      "created_at": "2023-02-09T16:49:43.633Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Gloomweaver vs. Benchmark, the Scholar, Ra, Tempest and Nightmist at the Court of Blood in the gloomiest month of the year. Somehow it seems this should have taken place in St. Louis- we need a new location deck!</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/f/fb491913678632ad9286cd15f5c4f435c8d3809d.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/fb491913678632ad9286cd15f5c4f435c8d3809d\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/fb491913678632ad9286cd15f5c4f435c8d3809d_2_231x500.jpeg\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"zQYsjDX5FwksgQQaXcUd6CleL7f\" width=\"231\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/fb491913678632ad9286cd15f5c4f435c8d3809d_2_231x500.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/fb491913678632ad9286cd15f5c4f435c8d3809d_2_346x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/fb491913678632ad9286cd15f5c4f435c8d3809d_2_462x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/fb491913678632ad9286cd15f5c4f435c8d3809d_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">828×1792 108 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>Nothing too much to say here- February is harder to get through than Gloomweaver, especially with this bunch. I honestly think Benchmark could have soloed this himself. I did very much appreciate Scholar using Alchemical Redirection to help out Nightmist who could cast multiple Heedless Lashes and Oblivion and then draw more cards without any recourse. With Tempest’s Reclaim from the Deep, that set up 3 turns with Nightmist unleashing at full power. There was really nothing Gloomweaver could do to save itself here, and like February, it too will be over no matter how hard it tries.</p>",
